From d1f6a2b7c623ba6feee3cb1e5be28702e22d9d47 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: g1-door <g1-door@local>
Date: Fri, 6 Nov 2026 09:35:15 +0900
Subject: [PATCH] door: optionally cap the shoulder roll push into the torso
 and penalize it (env.config.shoulder_roll_press_max_nm pulls the sent
 shoulder roll target back so that kp*(target minus angle) toward the torso
 stays within the limit, the same as the real robot
 door_run_stock.cap_roll_press, leaving the outward side, the other joints,
 the accumulator and the observations alone;
 rewards.reward_scales.penalty_shoulder_roll_press penalizes the squared
 torque toward the torso, averaged over physics substeps, since the motor heat
 grows with it; on 11-06 the real robot pushed the left arm into the torso at
 20 N*m and reached 88 C in 6 s; default off = unchanged) (11-06)

